Original commit body from f784bc332e4cdbbdde25de5e074f49952cd8908c:

Path(".github_deploy").suffix is "" -- a leading dot is not an extension --
so shellcheck's two extensionless bash scripts were read as an unknown
language. That silently skipped the bash-only branch listing ambient
parameter expansions, and the packet printed

    (none found; searched .github_deploy 1-28)

for a file whose line 11 reads `for tag in $TAGS`. It is the defect WI-rudin
exists to close, arriving through a different door: the listing is empty not
because the read is absent but because the instrument never looked, and the
absence points an adjudicator toward FALSE POSITIVE.

_language_of now consults the shebang when the extension resolves to nothing,
in the one home both the source and the sink listing read. The extension
still wins -- it is the author's declaration about the whole file, where a
shebang says only how one entry point is executed -- and an unknown
interpreter resolves to "" exactly as an unknown extension does.

Found by reading the 26 rendered packets of measurement 0007 back against
source. Four carried an empty source listing; two are this defect and two are
honest (spacedrive's combine_files reads no environment variable in its span;
rabbitmq's rabbit_channel.erl span 2743-2744 holds no get_env call). Telling
those apart is only possible because the listing names what was searched.

